# Runtime state files that may be real files (pre-setup-state-dir.sh) or
# symlinks to ~/.autonomous-forever-state/.  Either way, never commit them.
#
# No trailing slash on the directory entries, deliberately. A pattern ending in
# `/` only matches a real directory, and setup-state-dir.sh creates these as
# symlinks — a symlink to a directory is not a directory as far as gitignore is
# concerned, so `blackboard/` left the symlink showing up as untracked. The
# slashless spelling matches both forms.
.autonomous-team/state.db
.autonomous-team/state.db-shm
.autonomous-team/state.db-wal
.autonomous-team/stats.duckdb
.autonomous-team/audit.jsonl
.autonomous-team/circuit-breaker-history.jsonl
.autonomous-team/external-intake-baselines.json
.autonomous-team/blackboard

# The same runtime-state files, at the repo root. Every one of these paths is
# derived from the state dir, and the state dir is whatever
# AUTONOMOUS_TEAM_STATE_DIR says it is — a relative (or empty) value resolves
# against the process cwd, which for anything launched from the repo root is
# right here. That is how a 4.4 MB DuckDB file ended up stageable by
# `git add -A`, invisible to `git status --untracked-files=no`.
#
# Leading slash on every entry so they anchor to the repo root and cannot match
# a nested path: `blackboard` unanchored would also swallow backend/blackboard.py.
/state.db
/state.db-shm
/state.db-wal
/stats.duckdb
/audit.jsonl
/circuit-breaker-history.jsonl
/external-intake-baselines.json
/blackboard

# KPI E2E test screenshots (runtime artifacts, not committed)
dashboard/e2e/__artifacts__/

# pytest-testmon per-worktree DBs (never commit — one per worktree/branch)
.testmondata*

